e reboot (cmd-2a5157a260484820). No unnecessary mutations, abandoned files, or failed services were observed. The lifecycle diff shows only the expected boot_id-tagged systemd-private temp directories churning across the reboot, which is normal OS behavior, not executor residue. Package health and failed-services checks remained clean before and after.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5382cb63cff040a8","cmd-09159f18fbad4b00","cmd-2a5157a260484820","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The executor created a self-signed CA named 'OS Comparison Root CA' on node1 and installed it into the system trust store via update-ca-certificates, verified with openssl verify returning OK. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also completed correctly: a pre-restart boot_id baseline, a reboot acknowledgement, a confirmed different post-restart boot_id (cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots), and post-reboot verification that the CA certificate and its trust status survived intact. No unnecessary mutations or residue were found.","limitations":["Trust verification relied on openssl verify against the system CA bundle rather than a live TLS handshake against a certificate signed by this new CA, though this is a standard and sufficient method to confirm system-level trust.","The full command trace showed only 12 commands; earlier discovery commands (cmd-d6acfe0b7a424acc, cmd-90aeb32aa0074639) were read-only and appropriately excluded from mutation review."]},"ttft_ms":5431,"type":"result","duration_ms":28614,"uuid":"62a06db8-67f1-4449-b7f2-8d880ae8fcbd","ttft_stream_ms":813,"time_to_request_ms":210,"first_content_frame_ms":813,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
